<title>FRANCE: Elf says no talks on Sanofi merger.</title>
<headline>Elf says no talks on Sanofi merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French energy group Elf Aquitaine said on Thursday it was not currently in merger talks for its pharmaceuticals unit Sanofi.</p>
<p>&quot;We have announced that we are putting Sanofi in a position in which to form alliances. We are opening another window of opportunity so the company can grow more strongly but there are no negotiations in progress at the moment,&quot; an Elf spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Elf earlier said it would be desirable for Sanofi to merge with other laboratories to boost its profitability and that Elf would not insist on holding a majority stake as a prerequisite.</p>
</text>
